{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/813904-promethean-advantages-in-2e","id":813904,"title":"Promethean advantages in 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-21T21:40:00-08:00","id":813904,"title":"Promethean advantages in 2e","content":"In the original write-ups of all the splats, one of the big things Prometheans had going for them (among the many, MANY things they didn't) was how tough it was for something to actually kill them. Unless you set them on fire, basically nothing could stop them. No wound penalties. No falling unconscious from bashing or lethal damage. And if you did manage to kill them, they'd just come back (Sometimes more than once.) They just didn't quit.<br /> <br /> Comparing 1e Prometheans to the 2e splats that have come out, the others give them a run for their money in that department though. Vampires only taking bashing damage arguably makes them harder to kill than Prometheans, who you could at least do lethal to in order to expedite the process. Werewolves can heal all non-aggravated damage every single round when they're in Gauru form, meaning it's really going to take either silver or a level of force comparable to an rpg in order to put them down. <br /> <br /> I haven't read through all of the spoilers for Promethean, but do we know if survivability is still going to be their focus? Because if they're going to focus on it to the point where it's their specialty or their thing that they do better than the other splats, I can't imagine much anything existing that could give them pause. Or are their abilities getting refocused to something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T21:57:48-08:00","id":813911,"title":"","content":"It doesn't make much sense if Frankenstein's Monster gets killed by the torch-wielding mob.<br /> <br /> Promethean is a game about the journey, one that's specifically painful, hostile, and unpleasant, but those physical dangers are there to hammer home the philosophical beats; you don't learn anything if you get beaten to death, but you learn a lot if you get beaten /close/ to death and then have time to reflect on human cruelty and your outsider nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T01:20:55-08:00","id":813984,"title":"","content":"I think Prometheans are still tougher than most. Vampires have only slightly closed the gap. Werewolves are a much larger threat, especially if Disquiet continues to affect them. Still, a Promethean can come back from death, and the previews indicate that they actually must die once before the New Dawn, so that's still operative.<br /> <br /> So, Prometheans are less tough in comparison with newer revisions, but they are still brutally tough, and always have been. Their stories don't suffer for their invulnerability, which meant to isolate them from the mortals they wish to join.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T04:58:59-08:00","id":814049,"title":"","content":"Also, nothing tells us that they won't have the same advantages as a vampire. After all, they don't really need their internal organs as long as the Divine Fire burns within them.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they'll have some other powers to make them even more resilient.<br /> <br /> And yeah comparing any splat from first to any splat from second will be... brutally one-sided in terms of power-level","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:",